  "verbalization": "Carmustine, a chemotherapy agent, is implicated in the treatment of mantle cell lymphoma through a chain of indications involving vincristine. The evidence suggests that Carmustine may be repurposed for mantle cell lymphoma, as it is linked to diffuse large B-cell lymphoma of the central nervous system and plasmablastic lymphoma, both of which are associated with vincristine. Vincristine, in turn, is indicated for mantle cell lymphoma, forming a potential pathway where Carmustine could exert its therapeutic effect. The shared use of vincristine in these conditions implies a possible mechanism of action that is relevant to mantle cell lymphoma. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Carmustine to be a candidate for repurposing in this disease, provided further mechanistic validation is conducted. The evidence is supported by a consistent chain of indications, but the exact mode of action remains to be elucidated.",
